== Trivia ==
* {{dlc|na}} Despite Bonies being made entirely of bones, they leave bloodstains behind upon death.
** {{dlc|a}} They only leave behind bones when killed.
* Bonies are one of a few enemies in-game to have their own unique projectile type.
* Bonies were confirmed to be the [[boisite:84188046989|first enemy]] '''not designed''' by Edmund McMillen. He also confirmed that it was designed by Matt, the lead artist for ''The Binding Of Isaac: Rebirth'', and that Edmund loved the simplicity of the AI, fitting "perfectly into the Isaac world."
* {{dlc+|a}} Bonies are spawned by {{e|The Forsaken}}, and Black Bonies are spawned by its [[The Forsaken#Champion Versions|Black Champion version]].{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} Holy Bonies, {{e|Holy Mulligan}}s, and {{e|Holy Eye}}s originated as cards from the card game ''The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls''.{{dlc-}}
* Holy Bonies have the highest [[Stage HP]] among regular Monsters in the game.
* If a Maze Roamer spawns as a [[Champion]], its counterpart will be a Champion of the same type.
* The Maze Roamer's tactic of spawning in groups, lining up with Isaac, and mirroring the other Maze Roamer's movements are similar to the cut enemy [[anti:Gaper#Strifer|Strifer]], which appeared in Antibirth. The Strifer also appeared in Mausoleum, the alternate level to Gehenna.
* {{dlc|r}} The [[Anti:Revenant|Revenant]] first appeared in the ''Antibirth'' mod where it also had 2.4 stage hp.

